# Go source is LF, everywhere, on every platform.
#
# 34 of the repo's .go files were checked in with CRLF line terminators.
# gofmt always writes LF, so every one of them was permanently "unformatted"
# as far as `gofmt -l` is concerned -- which is why CI had no gofmt gate:
# adding one would have reported 34 files that nobody had actually
# misformatted. That in turn meant real formatting drift in 8 other files
# went unreported for as long as it had been there.
#
# Normalising the endings and pinning them here is what makes a gofmt gate
# possible. Without the pin, a checkout on Windows with core.autocrlf=true
# reintroduces CRLF and the gate goes red for everyone on that platform.
*.go text eol=lf

# The Go toolchain's own files, and the formats where a stray CRLF is
# equally load-bearing.
go.mod  text eol=lf
go.sum  text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf

# Sample binaries and anything else binary must never be touched.
*.so    binary
*.bin   binary
*.png   binary
